content.text:
Now JS core changes. Let's plan edits precisely.

## app-core.js
1. Add new icons: search exists, lock exists, command maybe keyboard? We can use search. Add `arrow-up`, `arrow-down`? can use text. Add `copy` maybe. Add `link` icon maybe. For copy link button use `external`? We'll add `link`: `<path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.5.5l2-2a5 5 0 0 0-7-7l-1.1 1.1"/><path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.5-.5l-2 2a5 5 0 0 0 7 7l1.1-1.1"/>`. Also `alert` maybe. Add `cpu` maybe not. Add `layers`? Use existing.
2. FALLBACK missions add dependsOn (and maybe blocked derived later). Not all needed but parity. Add to existing 5:
   - onboarding []
   - events []
   - sync []
   - permissions ['mission-sync']
   - demo ['mission-onboarding','mission-events']
3. Add `syncMeta` after replay const.
4. normalizeState: ensure mission dependsOn arrays and add derived? We'll compute functions. Add:
```
data.missions.forEach(m => {
  m.projectId=...
  m.dependsOn = Array.isArray(m.dependsOn) ? m.dependsOn.filter(d=>typeof d==='string') : [];
});
```
Also ensure agents `lastHeartbeat` preserved.
5. Add helpers after `isOpen`:
```
const isMissionComplete = m => Boolean(m && (m.status==='done'||m.githubState==='closed'));
const missionDependencies = m => ...
const missionBlockers = m => ...
const isBlocked = m => ...
```
Careful `missionById` uses state.missions. Fine.
6. `eventAgeAt(e, at=replay.at)` helper. Where? after replay functions. Use in display files.
7. Route functions. Need insert maybe before navigation section. Variables `let activeDetail = null; let appliedHash = ''; const ROUTE_VIEWS...`.
   - `viewTitle` map perhaps for palette.
   - `parseRoute(hash)` robust.
   - `routeHash(view, kind, id)`.
   - `setRouteHash(view, kind, id, {replace})`.
   - `applyRouteFromHash(force)`.
   - `openRoutedDetail(view, kind, id)` calls openMission/openAgent/jumpToRoom. Function declarations hoisted across scripts? app-core loads before others but functions called after all loaded at boot; `openMission` defined in app-missions.js, available at runtime. Fine.
   - `navigate(view, options={})` modify to update hash, set `currentDetail`, close sheet when no detail, open routed detail. Need avoid `navigate` calling `openMission` which calls setHash etc. Let's write:
```
function navigate(view, options = {}) {
  if (!view) return;
  const changed = currentView !== view;
  currentView = view;
  if (options.updateHash !== false) {
    setRouteHash(view, options.detail?.kind, options.detail?.id);
  }
  // view toggling...
  ...
  if (options.detail && options.detail.kind) {
    activeDetail = options.detail;
    if (options.detail.kind === 'mission' && typeof openMission === 'function') openMission(options.detail.id, { updateHash:false });
    else if (options.detail.kind === 'agent' && typeof openAgent === 'function') openAgent(options.detail.id, { updateHash:false });
    else if (options.detail.kind === 'project') { activeRoom = options.detail.id; ... }
  } else if (activeDetail) {
    activeDetail = null;
    closeSheet({ updateHash: false }); // hash already base
  }
  if (changed) scroll...
}
```
But careful: `navigate('missions')` when sheet open from mission should close sheet. Good.
- `openSheet` doesn't need change.
- `closeSheet(options={})`: if activeDetail and updateHash!==false -> setRouteHash(currentView, null, null, {replace:true}); activeDetail=null; then close.
- `openMission`/`openAgent` need to call `setRouteHash(currentView, 'mission', id)` and set activeDetail. But they are in other files. We can add a generic `markDetail(kind, id, updateHash=true)` helper:
```
function markDetail(kind, id) {
  activeDetail = {kind,id};
  setRouteHash(currentView, kind, id);
}
```
Then openMission calls `markDetail('mission', m.id)` after found. openAgent similarly. `jumpToRoom` maybe set route? It calls navigate('world') then modifies activeRoom; we can add `setRouteHash('world','project',projectId)` and activeDetail? But project isn't a sheet, no close. Maybe avoid detail model for project. Hash could `#/world/project/id`; route apply sets activeRoom. Keep simpler: `jumpToRoom` calls navigate('world', {detail:{kind:'project',id:projectId}})`? But navigate's detail handling for project should set activeRoom, not activeDetail. Hmm. We can omit room deep links for now, or support via `activeDetail` kind project that doesn't open sheet. closeSheet would then clear. Fine:
   - parseRoute handles `project`.
   - apply route: if kind project, navigate('world', { detail:{kind:'project',id}}).
   - navigate detail project: set activeRoom=id, update room chips/classes, activeDetail null? Actually no sheet; don't set activeDetail. Hash remains. If navigating away, base hash changes. Good.
   - jumpToRoom: `navigate('world', { detail: projectId ? {kind:'project', id:projectId} : null})`; but navigate calls renderWorld before? It will set activeRoom before? Add in navigate before render:
     ```
     if (options.detail?.kind === 'project') { activeRoom = options.detail.id; ... }
     ```
     and remove manual code from jumpToRoom. But clicking room chip uses data-room-filter, no hash. Fine.
   - We could skip project deep links to reduce scope, but easy.
- `applyRouteFromHash(force=false)`:
```
function applyRouteFromHash(force = false) {
  const raw = location.hash;
  if (!force && raw === appliedHash) return;
  appliedHash = raw;
  const route = parseRoute(raw);
  navigate(route.view, { updateHash: false, detail: route.detail });
}
```
When navigate updateHash false, it doesn't update appliedHash. Fine.
- `setRouteHash`:
```
function setRouteHash(view, kind, id, options={}) {
  const hash = routeHash(view, kind, id);
  appliedHash = hash;
  if (location.hash === hash) return;
  if (options.replace) history.replaceState(null, '', hash);
  else location.hash = hash;
}
```
Setting location.hash triggers hashchange; handler sees `location.hash === appliedHash` true -> return. Great.
- `routeHash` ensure id encoded: `encodeURIComponent(id)`.
- `parseRoute` decode.
```
function parseRoute(hash='') {
 const clean = String(hash).replace(/^#\/?/, '');
 if (!clean) return {view:'home',detail:null};
 const parts = clean.split('/').filter(Boolean).map(decodeURIComponent);
 const views = ['home','world','missions','agents','plan'];
 let view = views.includes(parts[0]) ? parts.shift() : 'home';
 // support #mission/id
 if (['mission','agent','project'].includes(parts[0])) {
   const kind = parts.shift();
   const id=parts.shift();
   const map={mission:'missions',agent:'agents',project:'world'};
   if (!views.includes(clean.split('/')[0])) view=map[kind];
   return {view, detail:id?{kind,id}:null};
 }
 if (['mission','agent','project'].includes(parts[1]) && parts[0]) ...
```
Simplify:
```
const views = [...];
const first = parts[0];
let view = views.includes(first) ? first : 'home';
let rest = views.includes(first) ? parts.slice(1) : parts;
if (['mission','agent','project'].includes(rest[0]) && rest[1]) {
  const kind=rest[0], id=rest[1];
  if (!views.includes(first)) view = {mission:'missions',agent:'agents',project:'world'}[kind];
  return {view, detail:{kind,id}};
}
return {view, detail:null};
```
Supports `#/missions/mission/id`, `#/mission/id`, `#/agents/agent/id`, `#/world/project/id`.
- Boot: after initial render, `applyRouteFromHash(true);` and if no hash maybe `history.replaceState(null,'',routeHash('home'))`; but applyRouteFromHash with no hash -> navigate home. If we then replace state to #/home maybe nice. Do:
```
if (!location.hash) { appliedHash='#/home'; history.replaceState(null,'','#/home'); }
applyRouteFromHash(true);
```
But applyRouteFromHash force true with appliedHash already set and raw `#/home` -> no problem.
- `navigate` currently scrolls only changed. Keep.
- When detail sheet opened by card click from home, `openMission` marks currentView home and hash `#/home/mission/id`. Fine.
- When clicking mission card in missions, same currentView missions -> `#/missions/mission/id`.
- If `openMission` called from a dependency link inside sheet, it will markDetail again and open new sheet, hash updates push. Fine.
- Closing sheet uses replaceState to base, so back won't reopen. Good.
- If user opens sheet by direct link then closes, replaceState base. Back goes to previous page maybe. fine.
- Need hashchange listener in bindEvents.

8. `renderSidebar` could update with sync label maybe. Add `conexionSummary` includes last sync:
```
function syncAgeLabel(ts) { ... }
function conexionSummary() {
...
const bits=[]; if (github.live) bits.push('GitHub'); ...
if (syncMeta.snapshotAt) bits.push(`sync ${relativeAgo((Date.now()-...)/1000)}`);
...
}
```
But `relativeAgo` for >3600 shows h; okay. Maybe keep simple: if github.live and syncMeta.githubAt -> `GitHub · hace 12s`. Sidebar small text. Good.
Need `syncMeta` defined before functions. Add `const syncMeta = { snapshotAt:null, githubAt:null, trelloAt:null, refreshing:false, timer:null };`.
But app-core top-level const accessible in app-actions and app-missions (global lexical binding) yes.

9. Ops health render function could go in app-home.js, uses helpers. Add `renderOpsHealth()` there.

10. Palette functions could go in new `app-command.js` or app-core. Better add new file `app-command.js` to keep core manageable. But module order. Add script after app-plan or before app-actions. Needs state helpers. We'll create `app-command.js` with palette rendering/open/close. Add to index and bump? New file version 1. Or put in app-actions.js? It has bindings. Separate is cleaner. But user asked implementation; new file okay. We need ensure `renderAll` maybe calls `renderPalette` no. Palette only when open. Add `app-command.js?v=1` before app-actions. Update README frontend order maybe.

11. Ops auto-refresh functions in app-actions.js. Need `refreshLiveSources`, `renderSyncStatus`, timer. Add to boot.

12. Mission dependency functions core:
```
const isComplete = m => m.status==='done' || m.githubState==='closed';
const missionBlockers = m => (m.dependsOn||[]).map(missionById).filter(dep => dep && !isComplete(dep));
const isBlocked = m => Boolean(m) && !isComplete(m) && missionBlockers(m).length>0;
```
Potential seed state has `isBlocked` from coord but compute dynamic. Good.
Maybe `dependentMissions` for sheet? not needed.

13. `filteredMissions` update and toolbar counts.

14. `missionCardMarkup` add badge and class. Need CSS.
15. `openMission` dependencies section and copy link. Also update recent age.
16. `openAgent` markDetail/copy link + age fix.
17. `renderAgent` age fix.
18. `renderHome` ops block and age fix.
19. `renderWorld` age fix.
20. `renderPlan` blocked classes and mini plan lock.
21. `renderTrelloActions` no change.

Let's start app-core patches.

### app-core icons, fallback, normalize, helpers, route, navigate/closeSheet, sync meta/conexion
Use edit calls.

Add icons link/keyboard maybe. At end of ICONS before dot:
```
link: ...
alert: ...
```
Use search existing. Add `copy`? We'll use link.

Patch.

